{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJmewcugm4oWWvwSB82Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`python3 -m unittest -q` now passes (7 tests). I made three changes: two bug fixes in `household/bills.py` and one correction to a test.\n\n1. **`split_bill`**: it used `total_cents // people` for every share and dropped the remainder. It now uses `divmod` and gives the leftover cents one each to the first people, as the docstring says. Shares add up to the total, so `split_bill(1001, 2)` returns `[501, 500]`.\n2. **`due_dates`**: the month was `first.month + i` with no wraparound, so a schedule running past December hit month 13 and raised `IllegalMonthError`. It now rolls over into the next year.\n3. **`tests/test_bills.py`**: `test_three_ways` expected `split_bill(1000, 3) == [333, 333, 333]`. That sums to 999 and loses a cent, which contradicts the docstring and `test_remainder_goes_to_the_first`. I changed the expectation to `[334, 333, 333]`.\n\nThe third change edits a test rather than the code. If `[333, 333, 333]` was intentional, the docstring and the remainder test would have to change instead, so check that this is what you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":19233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":466},"output_tokens":389,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e6efed3-2903-4558-b421-bc2385664fa0","uuid":"3579288b-3db6-482e-87eb-c1876596be87","timestamp":"2026-11-22T22:40:04.764Z","request_id":"req_011ChJmewSzPfThzsVvyt5Do"}
